{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Ruby on Rails is a very powerful framework that is awesome at building RESTful APIs.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b0de5ebbe28b171e6037529e0daf9de44e2e01fbd1b50c9c7aeca7f7bf7c5b46.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.2], [6, 1.2, 1.64], [7, 1.64, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.34], [9, 2.34, 2.5], [10, 2.5, 2.86], [11, 2.86, 3.08], [12, 3.08, 3.3], [13, 3.3, 3.82], [14, 3.82, 4.2]]}, {"text": "Using vanilla rails to build an API, while completely possible, is not always the best way to go.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/cd93ef3aea333a3e12790b2c6851e6823a247d68d2784add0ae59fbbcc86b57a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.64], [2, 0.64, 1.02], [3, 1.02, 1.26], [6, 1.48, 1.88], [7, 1.88, 2.18], [8, 2.18, 2.64], [9, 2.64, 3.18], [10, 3.18, 3.42], [11, 3.42, 3.6], [12, 3.6, 3.88], [13, 3.88, 4.08], [14, 4.08, 4.3], [15, 4.3, 4.5], [16, 4.5, 4.66], [17, 4.66, 4.86]]}, {"text": "Grape is micro-api framework design to work along side rails for developing an RESTful API.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d5fcde582ebf726e1fecd8591c49333703cba635c2d1b1ddafe300d9f987eaef.mp3"}, {"text": "Grape has some very expansive documentation describing how the gem works, so I am not going to dive too deeply into that", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/11b76c5c4a2edafcaa8db9bcc170b00b7a5929614e137593acfe0403563ffab8.mp3", "words": [[2, 0.48, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 2.08], [6, 2.08, 2.74], [7, 2.74, 3.1], [8, 3.1, 3.24], [9, 3.24, 3.42], [10, 3.42, 3.82], [11, 4.16, 4.4], [14, 4.64, 4.78], [15, 4.78, 5.0], [16, 5.0, 5.2], [17, 5.2, 5.44], [18, 5.44, 5.72], [19, 5.72, 6.08], [20, 6.08, 6.36], [21, 6.36, 6.58]]}, {"text": "Pros", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b629726cd0b7234801e4206158e2f3f01af19022d4ec31a955fc5ec72c680845.mp3"}, {"text": "Starting off with the positives: grape is great a creating and maintaining documentation.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/72b83f8d20c935248caf6972da813a786774316c0c91313556e735909359ff15.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.22], [6, 1.64, 1.84], [7, 1.84, 2.06], [9, 2.22, 2.54], [10, 2.54, 2.72], [11, 2.72, 3.06], [12, 3.06, 3.68]]}, {"text": "I love the grape-swagger gem allows you to easily generate documentation from you existing code base.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6f3c4b44453a24b2c6f35462d750781dc226a1e1d85c23c9b4df91a955d2a22e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.54], [5, 1.5, 1.68], [6, 1.68, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.34], [9, 2.34, 2.78], [10, 2.78, 3.34], [11, 3.34, 3.76], [12, 3.76, 3.94], [13, 3.94, 4.3], [14, 4.3, 4.6], [15, 4.6, 4.84]]}, {"text": "Since the documentation is generated, all of the code is self-documenting and you don’t have to maintain separate API documentation files.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/90b14e6fd5979a601618443d4c12b0ae989a7b3b334b80aa663c942b5d4c63ff.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.92], [3, 0.92, 1.3], [4, 1.3, 1.76], [5, 2.12, 2.28], [6, 2.28, 2.44], [7, 2.44, 2.54], [8, 2.54, 2.76], [9, 2.76, 2.98], [11, 3.96, 4.12], [12, 4.12, 4.24], [13, 4.24, 4.46], [14, 4.46, 4.58], [15, 4.58, 4.76], [16, 4.76, 5.04], [17, 5.04, 5.54], [18, 5.54, 5.94], [19, 5.94, 6.48], [20, 6.48, 7.06]]}, {"text": "Because grape has its own DSL, it makes creating APIs easy to read and understand.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f8896e1350644c19e50abb4d41316406772e1690f2007cb43058cd3024f8b760.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [2, 0.54, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.56], [6, 1.86, 1.94], [7, 1.94, 2.06], [8, 2.06, 2.44], [9, 2.44, 2.9], [10, 2.9, 3.38], [11, 3.38, 3.58], [12, 3.58, 3.78], [13, 3.78, 3.92], [14, 3.92, 4.36]]}, {"text": "This makes the code base easier to maintain for future improvements.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/279f406cbfa590e2bd71328f884f31dab7e00b7211d7a7108cb6d2cc9aff1e85.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.3], [9, 2.3, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 3.16]]}, {"text": "Plus it has its own opinion for how to create an API, which really help keep your codebase consistent.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f67b623c68a3290adc5d4bc0f9eac32a6dad56a497c919a0f4268b6dd96f6afd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.36, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.74], [8, 1.74, 1.86], [9, 1.86, 2.08], [10, 2.08, 2.26], [11, 2.26, 2.66], [12, 3.04, 3.24], [13, 3.24, 3.6], [14, 3.6, 3.86], [15, 3.86, 4.1], [16, 4.1, 4.3], [17, 4.3, 4.74], [18, 4.74, 5.34]]}, {"text": "grape gives you a uniform way to control API HTTP Headers.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4ee625594b93603646eea36f8ff55e1904fcd7d2abf2fb635a0a29a3601d2196.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.4], [6, 1.4, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.4], [9, 2.4, 3.06], [10, 3.06, 3.64]]}, {"text": "Rather than having to roll your own classes to manage the response headers, grape makes it easy to set them.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/11605fa2c2f75f5c475061a5b4de4fc7d6fd8d60839e2e76fc50ced23f1c93a9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.9], [8, 1.9, 2.26], [9, 2.26, 2.5], [10, 2.5, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 3.04], [12, 3.04, 3.42], [14, 4.28, 4.5], [15, 4.5, 4.66], [16, 4.66, 4.9], [17, 4.9, 5.08], [18, 5.08, 5.3], [19, 5.3, 5.48]]}, {"text": "Cons", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/888f900af800cdcbd6e947bed17fded4d9661d7ebf0cfc0bf47316d9b8bec67b.mp3"}, {"text": "Because grape is independent of rails, it takes a bit of finagling for it to play well with rails.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a41d7cb5aecf4ab974bb7dd4dfa1a0160c0a4343ca91b268380654a7bb9bbdeb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.3], [4, 1.3, 1.6], [5, 1.6, 1.8], [6, 2.46, 2.56], [7, 2.56, 2.8], [8, 2.8, 2.96], [9, 2.96, 3.08], [10, 3.08, 3.24], [12, 3.74, 4.0], [13, 4.0, 4.12], [14, 4.12, 4.22], [15, 4.22, 4.44], [16, 4.44, 4.64], [17, 4.64, 4.86], [18, 4.86, 5.14]]}, {"text": "You have to manually include rails libraries like ActiveRecord or ActiveSupport.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/101afe0b3a64aec7018f2ba074a98c7e36cdb2137f6884e931d234ccf3f76a22.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.28], [8, 2.28, 2.98], [9, 2.98, 3.14], [10, 3.14, 3.84]]}, {"text": "Since there is no ActiveSupport, it makes caching responses more difficult than it should be.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2544e8a0ead35de0d3974a9c840787aec13d3cdd1ec76e0a431b2eb8bff3050a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.78], [5, 1.78, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 2.06], [8, 2.52, 3.08], [9, 3.08, 3.38], [10, 3.38, 3.84], [11, 3.84, 4.14], [12, 4.14, 4.28], [13, 4.28, 4.42], [14, 4.42, 4.66]]}, {"text": "Because grape has its own DSL, there is a bit of a learning curve to understand how it wants you to create an API.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/829ae8f2799a500c6c07be9036060a28016748d5e92d196317515920ea4f84df.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [3, 0.86, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.84], [6, 2.06, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.36], [8, 2.36, 2.46], [9, 2.46, 2.6], [10, 2.6, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 2.8], [12, 2.8, 3.04], [13, 3.04, 3.3], [14, 3.3, 3.52], [15, 3.52, 3.92], [16, 3.92, 4.24], [17, 4.24, 4.36], [18, 4.36, 4.54], [19, 4.54, 4.74], [20, 4.74, 4.84], [21, 4.84, 5.1], [22, 5.1, 5.28], [23, 5.28, 5.66]]}, {"text": "If you have a firm understanding of ruby, it shouldn’t be that difficult for you to pick up, but it definitely takes a bit of getting used to.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/05534e88c089faad15cf3f0cbc6caa1db515b88a8f5a44bf9f7cf2141591e58a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 0.8], [5, 0.8, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.64], [7, 1.64, 1.82], [8, 2.36, 2.44], [9, 2.44, 2.7], [10, 2.7, 2.86], [11, 2.86, 3.04], [12, 3.04, 3.46], [13, 3.46, 3.68], [14, 3.68, 3.76], [15, 3.76, 3.84], [16, 3.84, 4.04], [17, 4.04, 4.3], [18, 4.72, 4.88], [19, 4.88, 4.96], [20, 4.96, 5.38], [21, 5.38, 5.68], [22, 5.68, 5.84], [23, 5.84, 5.96], [24, 5.96, 6.06], [25, 6.06, 6.22], [26, 6.22, 6.54], [27, 6.54, 6.82]]}, {"text": "While grape makes it easier to read and write your api, it does add another layer of complexity to your rails application.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b1e5141475a18e4b33ef76458a44ebe8c0d6b9e7a0785c28104615a25ac31e3c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [4, 0.8, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.52], [7, 1.52, 1.68], [8, 1.68, 1.84], [9, 1.84, 2.02], [10, 2.02, 2.44], [11, 3.1, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.36], [13, 3.36, 3.62], [14, 3.62, 3.98], [15, 3.98, 4.32], [16, 4.32, 4.52], [17, 4.52, 5.0], [18, 5.0, 5.3], [19, 5.3, 5.44], [20, 5.44, 5.64], [21, 5.64, 6.22]]}, {"text": "Conclusion", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4888e403da94f4096ce831f4178717ca07d3749347a8d426ba8b09313a16232c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.64]]}, {"text": "For now, I am going to stick with rolling my own APIs using “just”* the rails framework.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d5d69820063832e993ae79f670c28c4357eb838a1649d5b51dfa244b37c0304e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.46], [2, 0.6, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.02], [6, 1.02, 1.22], [7, 1.22, 1.38], [8, 1.38, 1.64], [9, 1.64, 1.86], [10, 1.86, 2.06], [11, 2.06, 2.42], [12, 2.42, 2.98], [15, 3.74, 3.96], [16, 3.96, 4.52]]}, {"text": "Being more pure rails, gives me more control over the api had has less “magic.”", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/888b88b56f5c6887100a01d87dbe2499906e889c17f1bfa199ebebd4d930f6e4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.58], [5, 1.58, 1.82], [6, 1.82, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.38], [8, 2.38, 2.72], [9, 2.72, 2.92], [10, 2.92, 3.22], [11, 3.22, 3.6], [12, 3.6, 3.9], [13, 3.9, 4.1], [14, 4.1, 4.62]]}, {"text": "If I need to bring on a new developer, they will not have to spend as much time getting up to speed on this new library.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/80bea31de5b7df3f1c8bff28240909a39550e92fe6337ae498b0589cc18981a7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.62], [4, 0.62, 0.78], [5, 0.78, 0.98], [6, 0.98, 1.12], [7, 1.12, 1.22], [8, 1.22, 1.54], [9, 2.06, 2.18], [10, 2.18, 2.3], [11, 2.3, 2.48], [12, 2.48, 2.72], [13, 2.72, 2.9], [14, 2.9, 3.12], [15, 3.12, 3.3], [16, 3.3, 3.46], [17, 3.46, 3.74], [18, 3.74, 4.0], [19, 4.0, 4.22], [20, 4.22, 4.34], [21, 4.34, 4.6], [22, 4.6, 4.86], [23, 4.86, 5.08], [24, 5.08, 5.24], [25, 5.24, 5.64]]}, {"text": "Plus, vanilla rails has an awesome caching tools that don’t need to be arm wrestled into the framework.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b5e9ed28cdbcec8bb8c5673dd6d03bef95c20d4fbd7f28e326c643944403a77f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [2, 1.02, 1.4], [3, 1.4, 1.6], [4, 1.6, 1.76], [5, 1.76, 2.04], [6, 2.04, 2.42], [7, 2.42, 2.8], [8, 2.8, 3.02], [9, 3.02, 3.28], [10, 3.28, 3.4], [11, 3.4, 3.54], [12, 3.54, 3.62], [13, 3.62, 3.82], [14, 3.82, 4.22], [15, 4.22, 4.4], [16, 4.4, 4.54], [17, 4.54, 4.82]]}, {"text": "By “just” I mean, standard gem stack provided in rails 4.2 with typical basic additions I would use in both grape and vanilla rails.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/73d08d0491da7690b5d8ec9476170e9595069faf4697adff1fc327a6cd3a8cdc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.58], [2, 0.84, 0.96], [3, 0.96, 1.18], [7, 2.14, 2.56], [8, 2.56, 2.8], [9, 2.8, 2.96], [11, 3.74, 3.98], [12, 3.98, 4.3], [13, 4.3, 4.62], [14, 4.62, 5.04], [15, 5.04, 5.36], [16, 5.36, 5.5], [17, 5.5, 5.7], [18, 5.7, 5.84], [19, 5.84, 6.02], [21, 6.28, 6.54], [22, 6.54, 6.78], [23, 6.78, 7.1]]}]}